    "One table, different rows: query-time row access policies",
    "Filter rows by the caller's identity without making a separate table per team.",
    "Certification focus · cycle 3, position 2",
    '''<p>A hotel clerk may open the same booking system as a regional manager, but should see fewer rooms. The table does not change; the <strong>visible result</strong> changes with the caller.</p><p>A row policy is a predicate evaluated at query time. It does not grant table access by itself. First the caller needs ordinary object privileges; then the policy removes rows that are outside that caller's allowed region.</p>''',
    '''<p>The table contains orders <code>east-42</code>, <code>west-77</code>, and <code>east-99</code>. The group <code>east_analysts</code> receives two east rows. <code>west_analysts</code> receives one west row. A governance administrator may receive all three. The physical rows are unchanged.</p>''',
    {"when":"Use row-level policy when many users query the same governed table but each user or role may see only a subset of rows.","example":"Regional finance teams share one orders table; east analysts must never receive west customer records.","decision":"Choose a centralized policy when the rule repeats across many tables; use a table-level rule for narrow table-specific logic. Prefer separate datasets when legal or operational isolation requires a stronger physical boundary."},
    "Switch the active identity. Predict which order cards survive the policy before revealing the result.",
    "The browser filters three synthetic rows locally. It does not execute Unity Catalog or Snowflake, prove that identity groups are configured correctly, model policy-owner privileges, prevent inference through every query, or measure policy cost. Vendor SQL is sourced but not executed.",
    '''<div id="world"><label>Caller <select id="policyCaller"><option value="east">east analyst</option><option value="west">west analyst</option><option value="admin">governance admin</option></select></label><div id="policyWorld" class="world" aria-live="polite"></div></div>''',
    "const policyRows=[['east-42','east'],['west-77','west'],['east-99','east']];function paintPolicy(){const who=policyCaller.value;policyWorld.innerHTML='<div class=records>'+policyRows.map(r=>'<div class=\"record '+(who==='admin'||r[1]===who?'ok':'hidden')+'\"><strong>'+r[0]+'</strong><br>region='+r[1]+'<br>'+(who==='admin'||r[1]===who?'returned':'filtered before result')+'</div>').join('')+'</div><p><strong>Visible rows:</strong> '+policyRows.filter(r=>who==='admin'||r[1]===who).map(r=>r[0]).join(', ')+'</p>';};policyCaller.onchange=paintPolicy;paintPolicy();",
    [q("An east analyst has SELECT on the table. What does the row policy add?",["It removes rows whose predicate is false","It creates a new physical table","It grants SELECT"],0,"Object privileges allow the query; the row policy narrows its result."),q("Why test the policy as multiple identities?",["The same SQL must yield the intended different row sets","Policies run only for admins","Identity never affects evaluation"],0,"The security property is identity-dependent output."),q("What is outside a row policy's boundary?",["Physical isolation and every side channel","Filtering SELECT results","Using a row attribute"],0,"A logical query-time filter is not a separate account or storage boundary.")],
    [{"code":"rows = [('east-42', 'east'), ('west-77', 'west'), ('east-99', 'east')]","note":"Use one physical row set."},{"code":"caller_region = 'east'","note":"Represent the authenticated caller's authorized region."},{"code":"visible = [order for order, region in rows if region == caller_region]","note":"Apply the policy predicate before results leave the query boundary."},{"code":"visible_count = len(visible)","note":"The east caller sees two of three rows."}], {"visible_count":2},
    [["Databricks row filters and column masks","https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/filters-and-masks","Updated October 9, 2026"],["Databricks manual row-filter syntax","https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/data-governance/unity-catalog/filters-and-masks/manually-apply","Updated October 8, 2026"],["Snowflake row access policies","https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/security-row-intro","Living documentation"],["Snowflake CREATE ROW ACCESS POLICY","https://docs.snowflake.com/en/sql-reference/sql/create-row-access-policy","Living documentation"]],
    "The same three row cards stay in place while the caller changes. Cards become visible or crossed out at the policy boundary, so identity-dependent results are concrete.",
